  "decision": "Do not retain this implementation. Removing64KiB staging saves65,536B/op against the contemporary word baseline but adds declared extent/row/final state, without demonstrated CPU improvement. PostGCword raw cost is1.95%slower with separate confidence intervals; normalized intervals overlap. Two compressed controls have separated adverse historical normalized comparisons, not causal regression proof. These unresolved costs and extra format state do not justify acceptance of this allocation-only prototype in the current CPU roadmap. Preserve the lead; a materially revised storage design may be reconsidered without replaying unchanged sampling.",
